[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286696218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110468#issuecomment-3286696218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110468","id":3286696218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7D5wEa","user":{"login":"dmlary","id":857742,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzc0Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/857742?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-12T20:11:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T20:11:19Z","body":"One note, this may be related to #72281, but it's important to note that they're using the build-in shader editor.  They're also using compute shaders, but it's likely `RDShaderFile` under the hood too.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286696218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286724290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110468#issuecomment-3286724290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110468","id":3286724290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7D527C","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-12T20:22:52Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T20:22:52Z","body":"In Godot RDShaders are imported resources. When you run your game, you are not opening the raw GLSL file and then parsing/compiling it. You are opening an imported resource that contains SPIRV and reflection data. So no matter what, you need to reimport the file in the editor before it can be reloaded in your application. It works the same with any other imported resource type. This is why you get an error message when trying to run a project without opening it in the editor first. \n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286724290/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286742893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110468#issuecomment-3286742893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110468","id":3286742893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7D57dt","user":{"login":"dmlary","id":857742,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzc0Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/857742?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-12T20:30:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T20:30:12Z","body":"That makes sense.\n\nIs there an API to kick off that generation cycle?\n\nI see RDShaderSource, so I can technically create it by hand, but I also know `RDShaderFile::parse_versions_from_text()` does all the parsing necessary to split the glsl into the individual shaders, and handles includes.  It doesn't look like that is exposed in GDScript at this time.  Maybe `ResourceImporterShaderFile` is?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286742893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286746518","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110468#issuecomment-3286746518","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110468","id":3286746518,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7D58WW","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-12T20:31:58Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T20:31:58Z","body":"> Is there an API to kick off that generation cycle?\n\nI don't think any of the importer code is exposed to GDScript. You'd have to dig into the importer a bit and see what is needed","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286746518/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286787881","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110468#issuecomment-3286787881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110468","id":3286787881,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7D6Gcp","user":{"login":"dmlary","id":857742,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzc0Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/857742?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary","html_url":"https://github.com/dmlary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmlary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-12T20:50:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-12T20:51:28Z","body":"Simple workaround for anyone who only needs vertex/fragment split from glsl.  This **does not support includes or anything fancy**.\n\n```gdscript\n## Read and split glsl from a file path; returns RDShaderSource on successful read/parse\nfunc _load_glsl_from_file(path) -> Variant:\n    var lines = []\n    if not FileAccess.file_exists(path):\n        push_error(\"_load_glsl_from_file() file not found: \", path)\n        return null\n    \n    var file = FileAccess.open(path, FileAccess.READ)\n    if not file:\n        push_error(\"_load_glsl_from_file() failed to open `\", path, \"`: \", FileAccess.get_open_error())\n        return null\n\n    while not file.eof_reached():\n        lines.append(file.get_line())\n\n    file.close()\n\n    var source := RDShaderSource.new()\n    source.language = RenderingDevice.SHADER_LANGUAGE_GLSL\n    source.source_vertex = \"\"\n    source.source_fragment = \"\"\n\n    var type = null\n    for line in lines:\n        if line == \"#[vertex]\":\n            type = \"vertex\"\n        elif line == \"#[fragment]\":\n            type = \"fragment\"\n        elif type == \"vertex\":\n            source.source_vertex += line + \"\\n\"\n        elif type == \"fragment\":\n            source.source_fragment += line + \"\\n\"\n\n    return source\n```\n\nTo use to hot-reload shaders:\n```gdscript\n    # load the shader\n    var shader_source = _load_glsl_from_file(glsl_shader_file)\n    if not shader_source:\n        push_error(\"failed to load shader source: \", glsl_shader_file)\n        return\n    var shader_spirv: RDShaderSPIRV = rd.shader_compile_spirv_from_source(shader_source)\n    if shader_spirv.compile_error_vertex != \"\":\n        push_error(shader_spirv.compile_error_vertex)\n        return\n    if shader_spirv.compile_error_fragment != \"\":\n        push_error(shader_spirv.compile_error_fragment)\n        return\n    shader = rd.shader_create_from_spirv(shader_spirv)\n\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3286787881/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]